"""

NUMERIC_RULE_HELP = """\
\b
Numeric-constant rule (R14, R16): a line with a numeric literal fails unless every non-exempt
literal on it is covered by a "// PORT SRC: <vendored path>:<line>" marker (on that line or a
contiguous comment line immediately above), or every literal on the line is exempt. More than
one marker may cover a line; each marker must match at least one literal on the line it covers,
and every non-exempt literal must be matched by at least one covering marker's cited line.
\b
Exempt literal set (closed): the integers 0, 1 and 2 and their negatives -- structural indices,
arities and strides, not transcribed constants. Every other literal, including every float,
needs a marker.
\b
Exempt positions (closed): inside a line or block comment; inside a string or char literal;
inside an attribute such as #[...]; inside a test file under crates/*/tests/ or a #[cfg(test)]
module.
\b
Both sets are closed. There is no per-module, per-file or per-line opt-out: no marker, no
allowlist file and no comment suppresses this rule. Noise on first contact with a real module
is answered by a pull request against port/port-status, never by the module.
"""


MARKER_WHITELIST_HELP = """\
\b
Marker whitelist (closed): every port marker is one of TODO(port):, PERF(port):, PORT NOTE:,
SAFETY:, PORT SRC: or FIDELITY(port):. A line comment that looks like a marker (an all-capitals
word, optionally "(port)", then a colon -- or, case-insensitively, the exact spelling of one of
